Q7 — Two VLANs: Sales VLAN 10 and HR VLAN 20
Topology:
R1 G0/0 <— trunk —> SW1 F0/1
SW1 F0/2–F0/3: Sales PCs; SW1 F0/4–F0/5: HR PCs.
Example subnets:
VLAN 10: 192.168.10.0/24, gateway 192.168.10.1
VLAN 20: 192.168.20.0/24, gateway 192.168.20.1

SW1:
enable
configure terminal
vlan 10
 name SALES
vlan 20
 name HR
interface range fastEthernet0/2-3
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 10
 spanning-tree portfast
exit
interface range fastEthernet0/4-5
 switchport mode access
 switchport access vlan 20
 spanning-tree portfast
exit
interface fastEthernet0/1
 switchport mode trunk
 no shutdown
end
write memory

R1 (router-on-a-stick; connect R1 G0/0 to SW1 F0/1):
enable
configure terminal
interface gigabitEthernet0/0
 no shutdown
exit
interface gigabitEthernet0/0.10
 encapsulation dot1Q 10
 ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
exit
interface gigabitEthernet0/0.20
 encapsulation dot1Q 20
 ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0
end
write memory

PC IP configuration (static example):
Sales PC0: 192.168.10.10 /24, gateway 192.168.10.1
Sales PC1: 192.168.10.11 /24, gateway 192.168.10.1
HR PC0:    192.168.20.10 /24, gateway 192.168.20.1
HR PC1:    192.168.20.11 /24, gateway 192.168.20.1

Verify:
show vlan brief
show interfaces trunk
show ip interface brief
ping between PCs in same VLAN and across VLANs.
